   - title: Optional probability variation
-    text: "Starting point: Finish the ghost-note comparison above with ghost trigs on steps 44 and 60. This is an optional, player-run probability exercise, not a reconstruction of the recording. At probability 50, each ghost onset may play or be skipped on each pass, so evaluate the range of outcomes over several loops instead of expecting a fixed recording.\n\n**Set a dependable main beat.** Select channel 1 and open Channel tasks → Trig params. Turn E2 to a slot, press K2, turn E3 to Trig Probability, press K3. With no step held, set the channel default to 100. Check: every main hit remains eligible on every pass.\n\n**Check both boundaries.** Move to the sixteen-step page for steps 33–48, hold step 44, set its probability to 0, and release. Move to steps 49–64 and set step 60 to 0 the same way. Play: neither ghost note sounds in bars 3 or 4; the main hits continue. Stop. Set both ghost steps to 100 and play again: both ghost notes play on every pass, matching the fixed comparison. Stop.\n\n**Try the optional variation.** Set steps 44 and 60 to 50 and play several loops. The musical result to listen for is a quiet pickup that appears on some passes and leaves space on others, while the main hits stay present. Which ghost hit appears can differ each loop; no particular pass or captured result is promised.\n\nRestore the fixed comparison by setting both steps to 100, or remove a lock by holding its step and pressing K2. For a captured 0/100 probability example, see Trig Probability, “Turn chance into explicit rests.”"
+    text: "Starting point: Finish the ghost-note comparison above with ghost trigs on steps 44 and 60. This is an optional, player-run probability exercise, not a reconstruction of the recording. At probability 50, each ghost onset may play or be skipped on each pass, so evaluate the range of outcomes over several loops instead of expecting a fixed recording.\n\n**Set a dependable main beat.** Select channel 1 and open Channel tasks → Trig params. Turn E2 to a slot, press K2, turn E3 to Trig Probability, press K3. With no step held, set the channel default to 100. Check: every main hit remains eligible on every pass.\n\n**Check both boundaries.** On the full Trig Params grid, hold step 44 at (12,6), set its probability to 0, and release. Hold step 60 at (12,7), set it to 0 the same way. Play: neither ghost note sounds in bars 3 or 4; the main hits continue. Stop. Set both ghost steps to 100 and play again: both ghost notes play on every pass, matching the fixed comparison. Stop.\n\n**Try the optional variation.** Set steps 44 and 60 to 50 and play several loops. The musical result to listen for is a quiet pickup that appears on some passes and leaves space on others, while the main hits stay present. Which ghost hit appears can differ each loop; no particular pass or captured result is promised.\n\nRestore the fixed comparison by setting both steps to 100, or remove a lock by holding its step and pressing K2. For a captured 0/100 probability example, see Trig Probability, “Turn chance into explicit rests.”"
