   - title: 'Build the recording: Average, then Higher'
-    text: "Starting point: use an empty project at 90 BPM, Rate /1, C major and playback stopped. Assign Polyperc 1 to channel 1, give it range 1–16 and assign patterns 1 and 2. Turn Lock merged to pent. Off.\n\nPrepare the two-slot comparison: Open Channel (3,8), select channel 1 on row 1, then use E1 for tasks and E2 to choose a task; K3 opens it. In Pattern Trig and Pattern Note, choose patterns from row 1 and edit their steps. On Masks, E2 selects a value row and E3 changes it; hold K1 while tapping a step to add a trig. Open Song (6,8), copy slot 1 to slot 2 by holding (1,1) and tapping (2,1), then select slot 2. Set the selected slot length to 32 with the length fader at (4,7). Set Song tempo to 90 in Song tasks → Tempo & feel; set channel Rate to /1 on Clock and apply with K3.\n\nPurpose: compare the same two source patterns under two note-merge rules. Average combines overlapping notes by their mean; Higher adds the range between their highest and lowest values to that mean. Notes from only one pattern should stay the same in both slots.\n\n1. In Pattern Trig, pattern 1, tap steps 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 and 13. In Pattern Note, set degrees 0, 2, 4, 2, 0 and 4 at those steps.\n\n2. In Pattern Trig, pattern 2, tap steps 1, 5, 9, 11, 13 and 15. In Pattern Note, set degrees 2, 6, 3, 3, 0 and 5. On the Note grid, row 7 is degree 0 and each row above is one degree higher.\n\n3. On channel 1 Masks, leave Note and Trig at X so the patterns supply pitches and trigs. Set Vel to 80 and Len to half a step. These are the recorded channel masks.\n\n4. Open Channel tasks → Merge modes. Select Strategy with E2 and turn E3 until the screen reads ALL. Select Note mode with E2 and turn E3 until the screen reads AVERAGE. Set Song slot 1 length to 32.\n\n5. Copy slot 1 to slot 2 and select slot 2. Keep its length at 32; on Merge modes choose Note mode and set it to UP (Higher). Play the slots in order, then stop and select slot 1 to restore Average.\n\nListen for: The trig pattern and notes from a single contributing pattern stay the same in both slots. Only notes where the patterns overlap change.\n\nRestore: Select slot 1 for Average. Keep Lock merged to pent. Off and Trig Merge All for this recording, then return to the separate course project.\n"
