   - title: Practice longer and shorter Decay envelopes
-    text: "Comparison purpose: keep the note pattern fixed while only the Decay envelope changes. This recipe has two clearly separate exercises: first replay the retained recording's relative lock gestures; then try the separate endpoint contrast. Use a separate project so neither changes your course arrangement.\n\nStarting point: use an empty project at 90 BPM, Rate /1 and playback stopped. Assign Polyperc 1 to channel 1 with range 1–16. In Masks set default velocity 70 and Len ½; add odd-step trigs and notes 1/48, 3/55, 5/52, 7/55, 9/48, 11/55, 13/53 and 15/55.\n\nControls and step map: press Channel at (3,8), select its number on row 1, then turn E1 to Channel tasks. Use E2 to highlight Device, Masks, Clock, Trig params or Harmony and K3 to open it. On Device use E2 for the row, E3 for the named sound and K3 to apply. On Masks, E2 selects Note, Vel, Len or Chd1/Chd2; E3 changes the value. Hold a step while turning E3 for a local exception, then release it. To add a trig mask, hold K1, tap that step and release K1. Steps 1–16 are row 4, 17–32 row 5, 33–48 row 6 and 49–64 row 7. Column is the position within that group. For Song slots, press Song at (6,8); slots 1–3 are (1,1)–(3,1). Hold the source slot, tap the destination and release; then tap the destination to edit it. Set Song Tempo to 90 and each channel Rate to /1, applying changes with K3. In Trig params, E2 selects a slot, K2 opens its assignment list, E3 highlights a parameter, K3 assigns it and K2 returns. Hold a step and turn E3 to set its lock. K2 clears a held-step lock.\n\nRecorded comparison — replay the captured relative gestures. Slot 1 is two bars (32 steps) with no parameter locks; it is the straight reference. Copy slot 1 to slot 2 and keep slot 2 at 32 steps. Open Channel tasks → Trig params and assign Decay to slot 1. In slot 2, hold step 1 and replay the captured +200-detent E3 gesture; release it. Repeat the +200-detent gesture on step 9 and release. Then hold step 5 and replay the captured +40-detent gesture; release it. Repeat on step 13 and release. Check: steps 1 and 9 form the longer-tail group; steps 5 and 13 form the shorter-tail group, while the note pattern stays fixed. The retained capture records these encoder gestures, not displayed Decay values, so do not infer absolute values. Play slots 1 and 2, stop, then select slot 1 to restore the plain line.\n\nSeparate endpoint practice — a contextual contrast, not a reconstruction. In Song set slot 1 to 32 steps with no parameter locks. Copy slot 1 to slot 2 and set its length to 32. In slot 2, hold step 1 and turn E3 anticlockwise until the displayed Decay reaches its 0.1 s minimum, then clockwise to the displayed 3.2 s maximum; release the step. Repeat the 3.2 s setting on step 9. Set Decay to 0.1 s on steps 5 and 13, releasing each step afterward. Check the Trig params readout for the long settings on 1 and 9 and short settings on 5 and 13. Play slots 1 and 2, stop and select slot 1. On your instrument, compare the tails while the notes stay in the same order; the reader did not listen to a captured sound example.\n\nRestore: Select slot 1 to restore the unmodified line. Stop and return to the separate course project when finished."
+    text: "Comparison purpose: keep the note pattern fixed while only the Decay envelope changes. This recipe has two exercises: compare longer and shorter Decay tails with relative turns, then try the 0.1 s and 3.2 s endpoints. Use a separate project so neither changes your course arrangement.\n\nStarting point: use an empty project at 90 BPM, Rate /1 and playback stopped. Make sure n.b. PolyPerc is installed and enabled using [Sound Sources with n.b.](#norns-sound-sources-with-n-b); assign Polyperc 1 to channel 1 with range 1–16. In Masks set default velocity 70 and Len ½. Add trig masks on odd steps by holding K1, tapping each odd step and releasing K1. Select Note with E2; for each odd step, hold it and turn E3 to set the absolute MIDI note: step 1=48, 3=55, 5=52, 7=55, 9=48, 11=55, 13=53 and 15=55. Press Channel at (3,8), select channel 1 on row 1, then tap Pattern 1 in the second-from-top grid row to assign it before playing; an empty project has no pattern assigned by default.\n\nControls and step map: press Channel at (3,8), select its number on row 1, then turn E1 to Channel tasks. Use E2 to highlight Device, Masks, Clock, Trig params or Harmony and K3 to open it. On Device use E2 for the row, E3 for the named sound and K3 to apply. On Masks, E2 selects Note, Vel, Len or Chd1/Chd2; E3 changes the value. Hold a step while turning E3 for a local exception, then release it. To add a trig mask, hold K1, tap that step and release K1. Steps 1–16 are row 4, 17–32 row 5, 33–48 row 6 and 49–64 row 7. Column is the position within that group. For Song slots, press Song at (6,8); slots 1–3 are (1,1)–(3,1). Hold the source slot, tap the destination and release; then tap the destination to edit it. Set Song Tempo to 90 and each channel Rate to /1, applying changes with K3. In Trig params, E2 selects a slot, K2 opens its assignment list, E3 highlights a parameter, K3 assigns it and K2 returns. Hold a step and turn E3 to set its lock. K2 clears a held-step lock.\n\nRelative-turn comparison — compare longer and shorter Decay tails while keeping the note pattern fixed. In Song, select slot 1 and set its length to 32 steps with no parameter locks; this is the two-bar straight reference. Copy slot 1 to slot 2 and keep slot 2 at 32 steps. Tap slot 2 before editing its locks. Open Channel tasks → Trig params and assign Decay to slot 1. In slot 2, hold step 1 and turn E3 clockwise by 200 detents; release it. Repeat the 200-detent turn on step 9 and release. Then hold step 5 and turn E3 clockwise by 40 detents; release it. Repeat the 40-detent turn on step 13 and release. Check: steps 1 and 9 form the longer-tail group; steps 5 and 13 form the shorter-tail group, while the note pattern stays fixed. These turns are relative to the current setting; the absolute Decay value shown depends on its starting value and your device. Select slot 1 before comparing the two slots. Play slots 1 and 2, then stop and select slot 1 to restore the plain line.\n\nSeparate endpoint practice — try the 0.1 s and 3.2 s endpoints. In Song set slot 1 to 32 steps with no parameter locks. Copy slot 1 to slot 2 and set its length to 32. Tap slot 2 before editing its locks. In slot 2, hold step 1 and turn E3 anticlockwise until the displayed Decay reaches its 0.1 s minimum, then clockwise to the displayed 3.2 s maximum; release the step. Repeat the 3.2 s setting on step 9. Set Decay to 0.1 s on steps 5 and 13, releasing each step afterward. Check the Trig params readout for the long settings on 1 and 9 and short settings on 5 and 13. Select slot 1 before comparing the two slots. Play slots 1 and 2, then stop and select slot 1. On your instrument, compare the tails while the notes stay in the same order.\n\nRestore: Select slot 1 to restore the unmodified line. Stop and return to the separate course project when finished."
