-    text: "Starting point: Use a separate empty project at 90 BPM, Rate /1 and C major, with playback stopped. Assign Polyperc 1 to channel 1 and Doubledecker to channel 2. Give each channel range 1–16.\n\n**Controls and map.** Press Channel at (3,8), select its number on row 1 and turn E1 to Channel tasks. Use E2 and K3 to open Device, Masks or Trig params. On Device, E2 selects a row, E3 selects the sound and K3 applies it. On Masks, E2 selects Note, Vel or Len and E3 changes the value. Hold a step while turning E3 for a local value; hold K1 and tap a step to add a trig. Steps 1–16 are row 4, 17–32 row 5, 33–48 row 6 and 49–64 row 7; the column is its position within that group (step 33 is (1,6), step 61 is (13,7)). Hold the first step and tap the last to set a channel range, then release. For Song slots, press Song at (6,8); slots 1–3 are (1,1)–(3,1). Hold the source slot, tap the destination, release, then tap the destination to edit it. On the length fader, (3,7) gives 13 steps and three taps at (8,7) give 16; (4,7) gives 32 and (7,7) gives 64. In Song Tempo and feel (E1 tasks, E2 task, K3), set Tempo to 90 and press K3. Set each channel Rate /1 on its Clock page and apply with K3. In Trig params, E2 selects a slot, K2 opens its assignment list, E3 highlights a parameter, K3 assigns it and K2 returns. Hold a step and turn E3 to set its lock; K2 clears a held-step lock. Stop before copying or editing an independent comparison.\n\n**Prepare the two patterns.** On channel 1, create pattern 1 with trigs 1, 5, 9 and 13; set their degrees to 0, 0, 4 and 0. Set channel 1 octave to -1, velocity to 70 and length to half a step. On channel 2, create pattern 2 with trigs 3, 7, 11 and 15; set their degrees to 4, 2, 4 and 6. Set channel 2 octave to 0, velocity to 60 and length to half a step. Checkpoint: in C major the bass is MIDI 48, 48, 55, 48 and the lead is MIDI 67, 64, 67, 71.\n\n**Slot 1 — intro.** In Song Editor set slot 1 length to 16 steps and mute channel 2 with K1 plus its selector (2,1). Check: slot 1 is one bar of bass with the lead muted.\n\n**Slot 2 — verse.** Copy slot 1 to slot 2, set slot 2 length to 32 steps and toggle channel 2 back on. Check: the two-bar verse has both parts; bass remains 48, 48, 55, 48 and lead remains 67, 64, 67, 71.\n\n**Slot 3 — outro.** Copy slot 2 to slot 3 and set slot 3 length to 16 steps. Set channel 2 octave to +1 and channel 1 Velocity to 40. Check: the one-bar outro keeps the same four bass pitches at lower velocity and raises the lead to MIDI 79, 76, 79, 83.\n\nPlay the three slots in order, then Stop and select slot 1. The arrangement is intro (bass only), verse (bass and lead), outro (higher lead and softer bass). This is a separate arrangement example; return to the continuing course project when finished."
